    {
      "text": "shake off the dust of your feet, Matt. 10:14 (Mark 6:11; Luke 9:5; Acts 13:51; D&C 24:15; 60:15; 75:20; 84:92). held him by the feet, and worshipped him, Matt. 28:9. wash his feet with tears, Luke 7:38 (John 12:3). Mary … sat at Jesus’ feet, and heard his word, Luke 10:39. Behold my hands and my feet, that it is I, Luke 24:39. Mary … wiped his feet with her hair, John 11:2 (12:3). He that is washed needeth not save to wash his feet, John 13:10. laid them down at the apostles’ feet, Acts 4:35. at the feet of Gamaliel, Acts 22:3. bruise Satan under your feet, Rom. 16:20. cannot say … head to the feet, I have no need of you, 1 Cor. 12:21 (D&C 84:109). till he hath put all enemies under his feet, 1 Cor. 15:25 (D&C 49:6; 58:22; 76:61, 106). feet shod with the preparation of the gospel, Eph. 6:15 (D&C 112:7). if she have washed the saints’ feet, 1 Tim. 5:10. his feet like unto fine brass, Rev. 1:15 (2:18). make them to come and worship before thy feet, Rev. 3:9. beast … his feet were as the feet of a bear, Rev. 13:2.",
